890-d310712-r253800028-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "In the feet of the Divine", "text": "Great experience while doing Puja here. The best thing to do is book your puja beforehand and reach the temple by 08:15 in the morning to have great darshan and puja experience. Must Must Visit and get Abhishek done", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "business", "stay_date": "2015-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "6292F7EDBA5C5E6E5858DDA365D7FD45", "name": "AashishSir", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/AashishSir", "username": "AashishSir", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/54/8b/4e/instof-v.jpg", "contribution_count": 5, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 494941, "location_name": "Indore", "location_name_detailed": "Indore, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2015-02-12", "published_at_date": "2015-02-12"}, {"review_id": 253668154, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r253668154-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Not for everyone but sooo fascinating as well", "text": "What an interesting  place! This is an open air crematorium alongside a beautiful temple that is listed in the UNESCO World Heritage List. You absolutely need a mask, preferably with a dash of perfume  as the smell can become unbearable at times ( not all the time) . The family is there and friends as well. The workers put the body on something like a stretcher and pile lots of wood and stray for a good and fast fire. The five elements, air, fire, water, earth ( ashes) and sky ( Heaven) are all released as a result and all take their original form. The burning takes about 3 hours.\n\nThe person who lights the fire is supposed to be the son of the deceased. If the deceased has no sons, then the closest male family member does this. The eldest son of a dead father and the youngest son of a dead mother fulfill this task. The husband takes this responsibility for his dead wife.\n\nThe photographs will tell you more.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2015-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "9B4427BA525DC7D9D694621C24B17C38", "name": "Nesligül D", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/NesligulD", "username": "NesligulD", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/eb/6d/default-avatar-2020-19.jpg", "contribution_count": 6539, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293974, "location_name": "Istanbul", "location_name_detailed": "Istanbul, Türkiye"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/53/7d/d0/pashupatinath-general.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/53/7d/d3/watching-the-ceremony.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/53/80/3a/burning.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/53/80/3c/temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/53/80/3d/the-other-side.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/53/80/3f/inhabitants-of-the-temple.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2015-02-11", "published_at_date": "2015-02-11"}, {"review_id": 253383255, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r253383255-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Divine", "text": "It was a divine experience to visit this temple. Felt great peace and a must visit for lord shivas devotees. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [],